==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*3 [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[St. Dober]] spawns as the boss after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Tarsiriel]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]] spawns.

==Strategy==
As long as you have [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Soractes]] in your lineup, almost anything will work fine. Add units with good damage or crowd-control against [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] of your choice, as well as [[Cat Combo|Combos]] ("Research" Effect UP works especially good to spawn more Ramens). Don't forget to pick [[Ototo Corps|Waterblast Style]] for your base to decrease St. Dober's [[Surge Attack|Surge]] damage if you upgraded it or, if you didn't, bringing [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|units with Surge Immunity]] and/or using Defense/"Resistant" Effect UP Combos might be a good idea.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]: Cosmo's 850 standing range, large nuke, Freeze, Knockback and even Curse (if talented) vs Angels allows him to destroy this stage.
*[[Dioramos (Uber Rare Cat)|Ascendant Dioramos]]: Dioramos can Slow and Knockback the Angels on this stage, vastly reducing their pushing power. His high health and bulk allows him to tank and land attacks easily despite being hit with St.Dober's Surge Attacks.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Kasa Jizo]]: Simply spamming Jizo on this stage will melt it with little issue. Attack or Research Up combos can make this faster.

==Trivia==
*Given the American theme of [[Stratospheric Pathway]], Prairie Harbor's Japanese name, Great Prairie Harbor (グレートプレーリー港 ''Gurēto Purērī Minato''), may reference the [[wikipedia:Great Plains|Great Plains region]] or [[wikipedia:Grand Prairie, Texas|Grand Prairie, Texas]]. [[Tarsiriel]] also bears a faint resemblance to American inventor and industrialist [[wikipedia:Peter Cooper|Peter Cooper]].

